==German==
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|welih|lang=goh}}, {{term|wilih|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|hwilīkaz|lang=gem-pro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈvɛl.çə/|lang=de}}

===Adjective===
{{head|de|adjective}} ''f and plural'', [[welches]] ''n'', [[welcher]] ''m''

# {{context|interrogative|lang=de}} [[what]]; noun modifier which indicates that the precise identity of the noun is unknown.

===Determiner===
'''welche''' ''f and plural'', [[welches]] ''n'', [[welcher]] ''m''

# {{context|interrogative|lang=de}} [[which]]; which kind of.
#: '''''Welches''' Hemd wirst du tragen?''
#:: ''What shirt are you going to wear?''
# {{context|interrogative|dated|lang=de}} [[how much]]; how great (used in an exclamation)
#: '''''Welches''' Talent er hat!''
#:: ''What talent he has!''

